Polymer Physics — MIT 3.063 (@mat-mit-polymer: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mat-sources) { r_5EPM1GX0YZDKN71N771PQCWQ5P
Edwin L. Thomas, MIT 3.063, Spring 2007. [Course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-063-polymer-physics-spring-2007/), [lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-063-polymer-physics-spring-2007/pages/lecture-notes/) and [assignments](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/3-063-polymer-physics-spring-2007/pages/assignments/).

Work the available lecture sequence and assignments progressively. The opening structural studies use chains, molecular distributions, conformation, glass transition and morphology; later thermodynamic, kinetic, mechanical and functional studies provide the preparation for the deeper sequence. Cambridge's Polymer Basics and the introductory chemistry reading supply a slower entrance.

The public lecture index and first 29-page lecture were inspected on 30 October 2026. Its cover says Spring 2007 despite a stale Spring 2003 PDF document title. The index links lectures 1–22; lecture 23 is a wrap-up without an attached PDF. Separately recommended commercial books and removed figures are not included in the public course. OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms have third-party exceptions. Keep files, media and external software as references.

**Return:** [Materials-engineering sources](../Sources.lingua#r_51JAH6DB4WV2HZAB69G21ZHSMK).
} r_5EPM1GX0YZDKN71N771PQCWQ5P
